WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.064
The results are strong in both regimes.

00:00:04.144 --> 00:00:08.207
On WikiText-103,

00:00:08.287 --> 00:00:12.351
RetoMaton matches the perplexity of kNN-LM while
skipping eighty-one percent of the searches,

00:00:12.431 --> 00:00:16.495
and even when it performs a search at every step it
still lowers perplexity,

00:00:16.575 --> 00:00:20.638
because the carried-over pointers reinforce the
correct neighbors.

00:00:20.718 --> 00:00:24.782
On the Law-MT domain-adaptation task the gains are
larger and much more robust: perplexity

00:00:24.862 --> 00:00:28.925
drops from twelve point three four to ten point four nine,

00:00:29.005 --> 00:00:33.069
and as more searches are saved RetoMaton's
perplexity climbs only very gently while plain

00:00:33.149 --> 00:00:37.213
kNN-LM's perplexity blows up exponentially.

00:00:37.293 --> 00:00:41.356
Overall the automaton either cuts perplexity by up
to one point eight five,

00:00:41.436 --> 00:00:45.500
or saves up to eighty-three percent of the searches
with no loss.
